+# 01: Place a Hold and see the Hold queue
+
+**What to build:** A Member can place a Hold on a Title whose circulating copies are all out, and the desk can see the Hold queue for a Title, first in line first. A Member whose Balance has reached the Hold limit (5.00) is Blocked from holds and can't place new Holds. In this ticket Holds only wait; nothing makes them Ready yet. See `.scratch/holds/spec.md`; use the vocabulary in `GLOSSARY.md` and say "Blocked from holds", never a bare "Blocked".
+
+Add the `Hold` record and `HoldStatus` enum to the lending models (exported from the package like the other models), `HoldNotAllowed(LendingError)` to the lending errors module, and `place_hold(member_id, isbn) -> Hold` and `holds_for(isbn) -> list[Hold]` to `LendingService`. Put the Hold limit in the policy module as a new per-action Balance limit, refused through the same check checkout uses.
+
+**Blocked by:** None (can start immediately)
+
+**Status:** ready-for-agent
+
+- [ ] `place_hold` returns a new waiting Hold dated today, with no `copy_id` and no `pickup_by`.
+- [ ] A Hold is refused with `HoldNotAllowed` when a copy of the Title is on the shelf.
+- [ ] A Hold is refused with `HoldNotAllowed` when the Title has no copy on loan or on the Hold shelf (no copies at all, or all withdrawn).
+- [ ] A Hold is refused with `HoldNotAllowed` when the Member already has a waiting or Ready Hold on the Title, and when the Member has a copy of the Title on loan.
+- [ ] `HoldNotAllowed` says why the Hold was refused.
+- [ ] A Member with a Balance of exactly 5.00 is refused with `AccountBlocked` (action "holds", limit 5.00); a Member with 4.99 can place a Hold.
+- [ ] A Member Blocked from holds keeps their existing Holds in the queue and can still borrow if not Blocked from borrowing; once a Payment brings the Balance below 5.00 they can place Holds again.
+- [ ] Child Members can place Holds.
+- [ ] `place_hold` checks in this order: Member exists (`MemberNotFound`) → Title exists (`TitleNotFound`) → Blocked from holds (`AccountBlocked`) → `HoldNotAllowed` rules.
+- [ ] A refused `place_hold` changes nothing: the Hold queue is unchanged.
+- [ ] `holds_for` returns the Title's waiting and Ready Holds in the order they were placed, including several placed on the same day; it is empty for a Title with no Holds; an unknown ISBN raises `TitleNotFound`.
+- [ ] A Member can hold any number of different Titles.
+- [ ] Tests go through the `LendingService` interface, driven by `FixedClock`. The existing suite still passes.
