+# 02: A returned copy is set aside for the first waiting Hold and collected through checkout
+
+**What to build:** When a copy of a Title with waiting Holds comes back, it goes to the Hold shelf for the oldest waiting Hold, which becomes Ready with that copy and a Pickup deadline. Only that Member can borrow it; they collect it with an ordinary checkout, which fulfils the Hold. Returns of Titles nobody is waiting for work exactly as before. See `.scratch/holds/spec.md`; use the vocabulary in `GLOSSARY.md`.
+
+Add `CopyStatus.ON_HOLD_SHELF`. Write the "pass a copy on" rule once (oldest waiting Hold becomes Ready and the copy goes to the Hold shelf; otherwise the copy goes back on the shelf), because tickets 03, 04 and 05 reuse it. Put the Pickup deadline rule in the policy module: the day the copy is set aside plus 7 calendar days, moved to the next open day if that is a closed day, using the same open-day rule as due dates. `return_copy` and `checkout` keep their signatures.
+
+**Blocked by:** 01 (Place a Hold and see the Hold queue)
+
+**Status:** ready-for-agent
+
+- [ ] Returning a copy of a Title with a waiting Hold puts the copy on the Hold shelf and makes the oldest waiting Hold Ready, with that `copy_id` and a `pickup_by` date.
+- [ ] A copy set aside on Saturday 7 March 2026 has a Pickup deadline of Saturday 14 March; one set aside on Sunday 8 March has a Pickup deadline of Monday 16 March.
+- [ ] Two copies coming back serve the first two waiting Holds in order.
+- [ ] Returning a copy of a Title nobody is waiting for puts it back on the shelf, as before.
+- [ ] `return_copy` still returns the closed Loan and charges any Fine, whether or not the copy is set aside.
+- [ ] A copy on the Hold shelf is not among the Title's available copies, can't be withdrawn (`CopyNotAvailable`), and any other Member asking to borrow it gets `CopyNotAvailable`.
+- [ ] The Member with the Ready Hold can collect the copy with `checkout`, on any day up to and including the Pickup deadline: the Hold becomes `FULFILLED` and the copy goes on loan with the usual due date.
+- [ ] Collecting applies every usual borrowing rule. A Member who is Blocked from borrowing or at their loan limit is refused as usual, nothing changes, and the Hold stays Ready.
+- [ ] `checkout` still checks in its existing order: Member exists → copy exists → Blocked from borrowing → copy available → loan limit.
+- [ ] `holds_for` shows Ready Holds ahead of waiting ones and leaves fulfilled Holds out.
+- [ ] Once a Member has collected, they can't place another Hold on that Title while the copy is on loan.
+- [ ] Tests go through the `LendingService` interface, driven by `FixedClock`. The existing suite still passes.
