+# 03: Cancel a Hold
+
+**What to build:** Staff can cancel a waiting or Ready Hold. Cancelling a Ready Hold releases its copy, which goes to the next waiting Hold or back on the shelf. Cancelling never costs the Member anything. See `.scratch/holds/spec.md`; use the vocabulary in `GLOSSARY.md`.
+
+Add `HoldNotFound(LendingError)` to the lending errors module and `cancel_hold(hold_id) -> Hold` to `LendingService`. Reuse the "pass a copy on" rule from ticket 02.
+
+**Blocked by:** 02 (A returned copy is set aside for the first waiting Hold and collected through checkout)
+
+**Status:** ready-for-agent
+
+- [ ] Cancelling a waiting Hold returns it with status `CANCELLED`, and it leaves the Hold queue.
+- [ ] Cancelling a Ready Hold returns it with status `CANCELLED`, and its copy goes to the next waiting Hold, which becomes Ready with a Pickup deadline counted from the day of the cancellation.
+- [ ] Cancelling a Ready Hold with nobody else waiting puts the copy back on the shelf, where anyone can borrow it.
+- [ ] Cancelling never adds anything to the Member's Account.
+- [ ] Cancelling an unknown hold id raises `HoldNotFound`.
+- [ ] Cancelling a Hold that is already fulfilled or cancelled raises `HoldNotAllowed` and changes nothing.
+- [ ] A cancelled Hold keeps the `copy_id` and `pickup_by` it had.
+- [ ] A Member whose Hold was cancelled can place a new Hold on that Title.
+- [ ] Tests go through the `LendingService` interface, driven by `FixedClock`. The existing suite still passes.
