+# 04: The daily job expires uncollected Holds and charges the No-show fee
+
+**What to build:** A daily job expires every Ready Hold whose Pickup deadline has passed, charges the Member a No-show fee of 1.00 (child Members never pay it), and passes the copy on to the next waiting Hold or back on the shelf. It returns the Holds it expired. See `.scratch/holds/spec.md`; use the vocabulary in `GLOSSARY.md`.
+
+Add `expire_holds() -> list[Hold]` to `LendingService`, using the clock's today. Put the No-show fee amount in the policy module. The No-show fee is a new kind of automatic Charge and goes through the same automatic-charge path as Fines, so the child exemption applies without a separate check; its Account entry should identify the Hold it was charged for. Reuse the "pass a copy on" rule from ticket 02.
+
+**Blocked by:** 02 (A returned copy is set aside for the first waiting Hold and collected through checkout)
+
+**Status:** ready-for-agent
+
+- [ ] A Ready Hold is not expired on its Pickup deadline and is expired by a run on any later day: its status becomes `EXPIRED` and it appears in the returned list.
+- [ ] The returned list is in queue order and is empty when nothing expires.
+- [ ] Each expired Hold charges an adult Member 1.00; a child Member's expired Hold charges nothing.
+- [ ] The No-show fee counts toward the Hold limit and the Borrowing limit straight away.
+- [ ] An expired Hold's copy goes to the next waiting Hold, which becomes Ready with a Pickup deadline counted from the day of the run; with nobody waiting, the copy goes back on the shelf.
+- [ ] A Hold that becomes Ready during a run is not expired by that run.
+- [ ] Waiting Holds never expire.
+- [ ] A run after one or more missed days expires every Ready Hold whose deadline has passed.
+- [ ] Running the job twice on the same day expires nothing and charges nothing the second time.
+- [ ] Cancelling an expired Hold raises `HoldNotAllowed`.
+- [ ] Tests go through the `LendingService` interface, driven by `FixedClock`. The existing suite still passes.
