+# Holds
+
+Status: ready-for-agent
+
+## Problem Statement
+
+When every copy of a Title is out, a Member who wants it has no way to get in line. They can only keep coming back to the desk and asking, and whoever happens to be at the desk when a copy comes back gets it. Staff can't tell who has been waiting longest, can't set a returned copy aside for anyone, and copies set aside informally sit on a shelf indefinitely when nobody comes for them.
+
+## Solution
+
+A Member can place a Hold on a Title whose circulating copies are all out. Holds on a Title form a Hold queue, oldest first. Whenever a copy of the Title becomes free (it comes back, a new copy is added, or a copy set aside for someone else is released) it goes to the Hold shelf for the oldest waiting Hold, which becomes Ready. The Member then has until the Pickup deadline (seven days after the copy was set aside, moved to Monday if that falls on a Sunday) to collect it, which is an ordinary checkout of that copy. Staff can cancel a Hold at any time before it is collected. A daily job expires Ready Holds nobody collected, charges the Member a No-show fee of 1.00 (never for children), and passes the copy on to the next person waiting. A Member whose Balance has reached the Hold limit (5.00) is Blocked from holds and can't place new Holds.
+
+## User Stories
+
+### Placing a Hold
+
+1. As a Member, I want to place a Hold on a Title whose copies are all out, so that I get a copy when one comes back without having to keep asking at the desk.
+2. As a librarian, I want a Hold to be for a Title rather than a particular copy, so that the Member gets whichever copy comes back first.
+3. As a librarian, I want placing a Hold to return the new Hold, so that I can tell the Member their Hold was recorded.
+4. As a librarian, I want a new Hold to be waiting, dated today, with no copy and no Pickup deadline yet, so that its state is clear from the record.
+5. As a librarian, I want a Hold refused when a copy of the Title is on the shelf, so that the Member just borrows that copy instead.
+6. As a librarian, I want a Hold refused when the Title has no copies in circulation (none at all, or all withdrawn), so that nobody waits for a copy that will never come.
+7. As a librarian, I want copies on loan and copies on the Hold shelf to count as "out", so that a Member can get in line behind someone whose copy is already set aside.
+8. As a librarian, I want a Member who already has a waiting or Ready Hold on a Title refused a second one, so that one Member holds one place in each Hold queue.
+9. As a librarian, I want a Member who has a copy of the Title on loan refused a Hold on it, so that nobody queues for something they already have.
+10. As a librarian, I want a Member whose earlier Hold on a Title was fulfilled, cancelled or expired to be able to place a new one, so that only active Holds count.
+11. As a librarian, I want a Member to be able to hold as many different Titles as they like, so that there is no extra limit to explain.
+12. As a parent, I want child Members to be able to place Holds, so that children can queue for popular books too.
+13. As a librarian, I want a Member whose Balance is at or above the Hold limit of 5.00 refused with the same "account blocked" error checkout uses, so that the desk handles both blocks the same way.
+14. As a Member, I want a Balance of exactly 5.00 to block me from holds and 4.99 not to, so that the limit is clear.
+15. As a Member who is Blocked from holds, I want my existing Holds to stay in the queue, so that owing money doesn't cost me my place.
+16. As a Member who is Blocked from holds but not Blocked from borrowing, I want to still be able to borrow, so that the lower limit only affects Holds.
+17. As a Member, I want to be able to place Holds again as soon as a Payment brings my Balance below 5.00, so that paying has an immediate effect.
+18. As a librarian, I want placing a Hold for an unknown Member to fail with "member not found" and for an unknown ISBN with "title not found", so that typos are caught the same way everywhere.
+19. As a librarian, I want `place_hold` to report problems in a fixed order (unknown Member, unknown Title, Blocked from holds, then the reasons a Hold isn't allowed), so that the error shown is predictable.
+20. As a librarian, I want a refused Hold to change nothing, so that a refusal leaves no trace.
+
+### The Hold queue
+
+21. As a librarian, I want to see the active Holds on a Title, first in line first, so that I know who is next.
+22. As a librarian, I want the Hold queue to include both waiting and Ready Holds, so that I can see who has a copy set aside as well as who is still waiting.
+23. As a librarian, I want Holds served strictly in the order they were placed, so that nobody jumps the queue.
+24. As a librarian, I want fulfilled, cancelled and expired Holds left out of the Hold queue, so that it only shows people still in line.
+25. As a librarian, I want a Title with no Holds to have an empty Hold queue, and an unknown ISBN to fail with "title not found".
+
+### Copies going to the Hold shelf
+
+26. As a Member first in line, I want a returned copy of the Title set aside for me, so that the next person at the desk doesn't take it.
+27. As a librarian, I want a returned copy to go to the Hold shelf only when someone is waiting, and back on the shelf otherwise, so that returns without Holds work exactly as before.
+28. As a librarian, I want returning a copy to give back the same Loan record and charge any Fine as it always has, so that the desk's return workflow keeps working.
+29. As a librarian, I want a copy set aside to make the oldest waiting Hold Ready, recording which copy and the Pickup deadline, so that the Member and the desk know what to collect and by when.
+30. As a librarian, I want the Pickup deadline to be seven days after the copy is set aside, moved to Monday if that is a Sunday, so that Members get a full week and never a deadline on a day we're closed.
+31. As a librarian, I want each returned copy to serve one waiting Hold, so that two copies coming back serve the first two people in line.
+32. As a librarian, I want a new copy added to a Title with waiting Holds to go straight to the Hold shelf for the oldest one, so that new stock serves the queue before the open shelf.
+33. As a librarian, I want a copy on the Hold shelf not to appear among the Title's available copies, so that the desk doesn't offer it to anyone.
+34. As a librarian, I want a copy on the Hold shelf not to be withdrawable, as with any copy that isn't on the shelf, so that a Ready Hold never loses its copy.
+35. As a librarian, I want a Title never to have a copy on the open shelf while someone is waiting for it, so that the queue is always honoured.
+
+### Collecting
+
+36. As a Member with a Ready Hold, I want to collect the set-aside copy by borrowing it as usual, so that collecting is just a checkout.
+37. As a librarian, I want collecting to fulfil the Hold and put the copy on loan with the usual due date, so that it becomes an ordinary Loan.
+38. As a librarian, I want anyone else trying to borrow a copy on the Hold shelf refused with "copy not available", so that it stays for the Member it was set aside for.
+39. As a librarian, I want collecting to apply every usual borrowing rule, so that a Hold is never a way round being Blocked from borrowing or the loan limit.
+40. As a Member who is Blocked from borrowing or at my loan limit when I come to collect, I want my Hold to stay Ready until its Pickup deadline, so that I can pay or return something and come back.
+41. As a Member, I want to be able to collect on the Pickup deadline itself, so that the last day really is the last day.
+42. As a librarian, I want checkout to keep reporting problems in its existing order (unknown Member, unknown copy, Blocked from borrowing, copy not available, loan limit reached), so that holds don't change what the desk sees.
+
+### Cancelling
+
+43. As a librarian, I want to cancel a waiting Hold, so that a Member who no longer wants the Title leaves the queue.
+44. As a librarian, I want to cancel a Ready Hold, so that a Member who won't collect can release the copy early.
+45. As a librarian, I want cancelling to return the cancelled Hold, so that I can confirm it at the desk.
+46. As a Member, I want cancelling never to charge me anything, so that telling the library early is never worse than not turning up.
+47. As a Member next in line, I want a copy released by a cancelled Ready Hold to be set aside for me with a Pickup deadline counted from the day of the cancellation, so that I get a full week.
+48. As a librarian, I want a copy released by a cancelled Ready Hold to go back on the shelf when nobody is waiting, so that it can be borrowed.
+49. As a librarian, I want cancelling an unknown Hold to fail with "hold not found", so that typos are caught.
+50. As a librarian, I want cancelling a Hold that is already fulfilled, cancelled or expired to be refused as "hold not allowed" and change nothing, so that history can't be rewritten.
+
+### Expiring uncollected Holds
+
+51. As a librarian, I want a daily job that expires every Ready Hold whose Pickup deadline has passed, so that uncollected copies don't sit on the Hold shelf.
+52. As a librarian, I want the daily job to return the Holds it expired, so that the desk can see who didn't turn up.
+53. As a Member, I want my Hold not to expire on its Pickup deadline, only from the day after, so that I really have until the end of the deadline.
+54. As a librarian, I want waiting Holds never to expire, so that people keep their place however long the wait.
+55. As a librarian, I want each expired Hold to charge its Member a No-show fee of 1.00, so that not turning up has a cost.
+56. As a parent, I want child Members never to be charged a No-show fee, so that children aren't put off placing Holds.
+57. As a librarian, I want the No-show fee to count toward the Borrowing limit and the Hold limit straight away, like any other Charge.
+58. As a Member next in line, I want a copy released by an expired Hold to be set aside for me with a Pickup deadline counted from the day it was released, so that I get a full week.
+59. As a librarian, I want a copy released by an expired Hold to go back on the shelf when nobody is waiting.
+60. As a librarian, I want a Hold that becomes Ready during a run of the daily job not to be expired by that same run, so that a copy passed on is never immediately taken away again.
+61. As a librarian, I want a run on a day the job was missed to catch up and expire every Ready Hold whose deadline has passed, so that missing a day does no harm.
+62. As a librarian, I want running the job twice on the same day to expire nothing the second time and charge nothing twice, so that a rerun is harmless.
+
+### Unchanged behaviour
+
+63. As a librarian, I want returns, checkouts, Fines, Payments and the overdue report to behave exactly as before for Titles nobody has a Hold on, so that holds don't disturb anything else.
+
+## Implementation Decisions
+
+- **Interface (fixed; other code calls exactly this).** On `LendingService`:
+  - `place_hold(member_id: str, isbn: str) -> Hold`
+  - `cancel_hold(hold_id: str) -> Hold`
+  - `expire_holds() -> list[Hold]`: the daily job, using the clock's today; returns the Holds it expired, in queue order.
+  - `holds_for(isbn: str) -> list[Hold]`: the active (waiting and Ready) Holds on the Title, first in line first.
+  - `return_copy`, `checkout` and `add_copy` keep their signatures and return types.
+- **New records** in the lending models module:
+  - dataclass `Hold(hold_id: str, member_id: str, isbn: str, placed_on: date, status: HoldStatus, copy_id: str | None, pickup_by: date | None)`.
+  - enum `HoldStatus` with `WAITING`, `READY`, `FULFILLED`, `CANCELLED`, `EXPIRED`.
+  - new member `CopyStatus.ON_HOLD_SHELF`.
+  - `Hold` and `HoldStatus` are exported from the package alongside the other models.
+- **Hold record over its life.** A waiting Hold has no `copy_id` and no `pickup_by`. Becoming Ready sets both. When a Hold ends (fulfilled, cancelled or expired) its fields stay as they were, so an ended Hold that had been Ready still shows which copy and deadline it had.
+- **Hold ids** come from the repository's sequential id generator with their own prefix (as Loans use `L`). The Hold queue order is the order Holds were placed; `placed_on` alone is not enough because several Holds can be placed on one day.
+- **New errors** in the lending errors module, both subclasses of `LendingError`:
+  - `HoldNotAllowed`: the Hold can't be placed or changed in its current state. It says why (copy on the shelf, no circulating copies, already has a Hold on the Title, has the Title on loan, Hold already ended).
+  - `HoldNotFound`: no Hold with that id; carries the id, like the other "not found" errors.
+  - Existing errors are reused where they fit: `MemberNotFound`, `TitleNotFound`, `AccountBlocked` (Blocked from holds), `CopyNotAvailable` (someone else asking for a copy on the Hold shelf).
+- **`place_hold` checks in this order**, and a refusal changes nothing:
+  1. Member exists (`MemberNotFound`).
+  2. Title exists (`TitleNotFound`).
+  3. Not Blocked from holds (`AccountBlocked` with action "holds" and limit 5.00).
+  4. `HoldNotAllowed` if: a copy of the Title is on the shelf; the Title has no copy that is on loan or on the Hold shelf; the Member already has a waiting or Ready Hold on the Title; the Member has a copy of the Title on loan. The order among these is not significant; each is a `HoldNotAllowed`.
+- **Hold limit** goes into the policy module's per-action Balance limits as a new action for holds at 5.00, refused through the same "blocked from" check checkout uses. It only gates placing a Hold.
+- **Passing a copy on.** One internal rule handles every copy that becomes free: if the Title has a waiting Hold, the copy goes to the Hold shelf and the oldest waiting Hold becomes Ready with that `copy_id` and a Pickup deadline counted from today; otherwise the copy goes back on the shelf. It applies to:
+  - `return_copy`, after closing the Loan and charging any Fine;
+  - `add_copy` (a new copy of a Title with waiting Holds goes straight to the Hold shelf);
+  - `cancel_hold` of a Ready Hold;
+  - `expire_holds` for each expired Hold.
+  This keeps the invariant: a Title never has a copy on the shelf while it has a waiting Hold.
+- **Pickup deadline** lives in the policy module: the day the copy is set aside plus 7 calendar days, moved to the next open day if that is a closed day (today: Sunday to Monday). It reuses the same open-day rule as due dates, so closed days are defined in one place. Worked examples (calendar of the test fixture, Monday 2 March 2026 onwards):
+  - Set aside Saturday 7 March 2026 → Pickup deadline Saturday 14 March.
+  - Set aside Sunday 8 March 2026 → Sunday 15 March → Pickup deadline Monday 16 March.
+  - A copy passed on after a cancellation or expiry counts from the day it is passed on.
+- **Collecting is `checkout`.** `checkout` keeps its order: Member exists → copy exists → Blocked from borrowing → copy available → loan limit. The "copy available" step now accepts a copy on the shelf, or a copy on the Hold shelf for a Ready Hold belonging to this Member; any other copy on the Hold shelf is `CopyNotAvailable`. A successful checkout of a held copy marks the Hold `FULFILLED`. A refused checkout changes nothing and leaves the Hold Ready.
+- **`cancel_hold`.** Unknown id → `HoldNotFound`. A Hold that is fulfilled, cancelled or expired → `HoldNotAllowed`, nothing changes. A waiting Hold becomes `CANCELLED`. A Ready Hold becomes `CANCELLED` and its copy is passed on. Never charges anything. Returns the Hold.
+- **`expire_holds`.** Takes the Ready Holds whose `pickup_by` is before today, as they stand when the run starts, and for each in queue order: marks it `EXPIRED`, charges the No-show fee, passes its copy on. Holds that become Ready during the run are not expired by it. A Hold is never expired on its Pickup deadline. Running it again the same day finds nothing new.
+- **No-show fee** is 1.00, kept in the policy module. It is a new kind of automatic Charge on the Account and goes through the same automatic-charge path as Fines, so the child exemption applies without a separate check. The Account entry should identify the Hold it was charged for, as a Fine identifies its Loan. It counts toward every Balance limit immediately.
+- **Withdrawal** is unchanged: only copies on the shelf can be withdrawn, so a copy on the Hold shelf can't be (`CopyNotAvailable`).
+- **Available copies** keep meaning copies on the shelf; copies on the Hold shelf are not included.
+- **Persistence.** Holds are stored in the repository, which stays the only persistence. Only the service changes Holds.
+- **Atomicity.** Every refused call (`place_hold`, `cancel_hold`, `checkout`) changes no state. Validate before mutating.
+
+## Testing Decisions
+
+- **One seam: the `LendingService` public interface, driven by `FixedClock`.** Tests place Holds, check out and return copies, move the clock, run `expire_holds`, and assert on the returned `Hold`/`Loan` records, `holds_for`, copy status via `get_copy`, `available_copies`, `balance`, and raised errors. Nothing tests the policy functions, the repository or Hold storage directly; those are internal details and must stay free to change.
+- A good test describes behaviour a librarian would recognise, e.g. "a copy returned on Saturday 7 March must be collected by Saturday 14 March" or "a Member who doesn't collect is charged 1.00 the day after the deadline". Use concrete dates on the fixture's calendar (START is Monday 2 March 2026; Sundays are 8, 15, 22 and 29 March).
+- **Prior art:** the existing loan and fines tests use the shared `service` and `clock` fixtures (an adult `ann` and a child `kid`; a book Title with two copies; a DVD Title with one copy) and `pytest.raises` for domain errors. The single-copy DVD is the natural Title for queue tests. Register extra Members inside tests where a queue needs more people. Follow the same style in a new test module for holds.
+- **Behaviours to cover:**
+  - Placing: refused while a copy is on the shelf; refused with no circulating copies (all withdrawn); allowed when the only copy is on the Hold shelf for someone else; duplicate active Hold refused; Member with the Title on loan refused; new Hold allowed after an earlier one ended; Hold limit at exactly 5.00 and not at 4.99; a Member Blocked from holds keeps existing Holds and can still borrow; error order including `MemberNotFound` and `TitleNotFound` ahead of `AccountBlocked`, and `AccountBlocked` ahead of `HoldNotAllowed`; refused calls change nothing.
+  - Queue: `holds_for` order across several Members; Ready before waiting; ended Holds excluded; empty for a Title with no Holds; unknown ISBN.
+  - Hold shelf: return goes to the first waiting Hold with the right `copy_id` and `pickup_by`; return with no Holds shelves the copy as before; two returns serve the first two in line; `add_copy` goes to the queue; a copy on the Hold shelf is not in `available_copies`, can't be withdrawn, and can't be borrowed by anyone else; `return_copy` still returns the Loan and charges the Fine.
+  - Pickup deadline: Saturday → Saturday; Sunday → Monday; collectable on the deadline itself.
+  - Collecting: fulfils the Hold and creates an ordinary Loan; blocked or at the loan limit at collection is refused and the Hold stays Ready.
+  - Cancelling: waiting; Ready with the copy passed to the next waiting Hold (deadline from the cancel day); Ready with nobody waiting shelves the copy; no Charge; unknown id; already ended.
+  - Expiring: not on the deadline, yes the day after; No-show fee 1.00 for adults, nothing for children; copy passed on with the deadline counted from the expiry day, or shelved; a Hold that becomes Ready in the run is not expired by it; catch-up after a missed day; a second run the same day does nothing; waiting Holds never expire; the No-show fee can block holds or borrowing.
+- The existing loan, catalogue, fines and overdue-report tests stay as they are, as a check that nothing else changed.
+
+## Out of Scope
+
+- Renewals. They come next (see Further Notes); nothing about them is built here.
+- Holds on a particular copy, or any choice of copy.
+- Notifying Members that a Hold is Ready.
+- A cap on the number of Holds per Member.
+- Waiting Holds expiring, or a "not needed after" date on a Hold.
+- Reordering the queue, priority Holds, or staff overriding who is next.
+- Pausing or suspending a Hold.
+- Changing an individual Pickup deadline.
+- Waiving or refunding a No-show fee, or any fee for placing a Hold.
+- Scheduling the daily job; this work provides the method the scheduler calls.
+- Reports or listings of Holds beyond `holds_for` (e.g. a Member's Holds or the Hold shelf).
+- Any change to the overdue report.
+
+## Further Notes
+
+- Vocabulary follows `GLOSSARY.md`: Hold, Hold queue, waiting, Ready, Hold shelf, Collect, Pickup deadline, No-show fee, Hold limit, Blocked from holds. Say "Blocked from holds" or "Blocked from borrowing", never a bare "Blocked". Avoid "reservation", "waitlist" and "pickup time".
+- ADR-0001 (Fines charged on return) is unaffected; a return that sets a copy aside charges its Fine exactly as before.
+- **Renewals are next, and this design must not make them harder.** Two rules are planned:
+  1. A Loan can't be renewed while anyone has a *waiting* Hold on its Title. Ready Holds don't count, because those Members already have their copy. So the service must be able to tell waiting Holds from Ready ones per Title; `holds_for` returns both, so renewals will filter by status. A Member can't hold a Title they have on loan, so their own Hold never blocks their own renewal.
+  2. Only Members who owe nothing can renew: any Balance above zero refuses it. With whole-cent amounts this fits the existing per-action Balance limits as a threshold of 0.01. A No-show fee will therefore block renewals until paid.
+- Open question for the renewals spec, not this one: ADR-0001 says a renewal charges lateness so far. Whether the "owes nothing" check comes before that renewal Fine (an overdue Member who owes nothing can renew, then owes the Fine) or after (an overdue Loan can never be renewed) needs deciding there.
