+# 01: Account with Manual charges and Balance
+
+**What to build:** Every Member has an Account. Staff can add a Manual charge with a reason to any Member's Account, and the desk can look up what a Member owes right now. This is the first slice of the overdue fines spec (`.scratch/overdue-fines/spec.md`); it introduces the Account that Payments, Fines and blocking all build on. Use the vocabulary in `GLOSSARY.md`.
+
+Interface on `LendingService` (fixed, other code calls exactly this):
+- `balance(member_id: str) -> Decimal`
+- `add_charge(member_id: str, amount: Decimal, reason: str) -> Decimal`, which returns the new Balance
+
+Add `InvalidAmount(LendingError)` to the lending errors module.
+
+Store the Account as a record of entries (Charges, later Payments and Fines), with Balance computed from them, in the repository. That way later tickets can link Fines to Loans. The exact storage shape is up to you. Add no public method beyond the two above.
+
+**Blocked by:** None (can start immediately)
+
+**Status:** ready-for-agent
+
+- [ ] A newly registered Member has a Balance of 0.
+- [ ] `add_charge` adds a Manual charge and returns the new Balance; successive charges add up (e.g. 2.50 then 1.25 gives 3.75).
+- [ ] `balance` reflects all Manual charges added so far.
+- [ ] Child Members can be given Manual charges like anyone else.
+- [ ] Any reason text is accepted and stored as given, without checks.
+- [ ] `add_charge` raises `InvalidAmount` when the amount is zero, negative, has more than two decimal places (e.g. 0.005), is NaN or infinite, or is not a `Decimal` (a `float` or an `int`).
+- [ ] `balance` and `add_charge` raise `MemberNotFound` for an unknown Member; `add_charge` raises `MemberNotFound` rather than `InvalidAmount` when both apply.
+- [ ] A refused `add_charge` leaves the Balance exactly as it was.
+- [ ] Tests go through the `LendingService` interface only, using the shared `service`/`clock` fixtures, in a new test module for fines and Accounts. The existing suite still passes.
