+# 02: Payments
+
+**What to build:** A Member can pay some or all of what they owe, and the desk is told the new Balance straight away. Payments can never exceed the Balance, so the library never holds Member credit. See `.scratch/overdue-fines/spec.md`; use the vocabulary in `GLOSSARY.md`.
+
+Interface on `LendingService` (fixed): `pay(member_id: str, amount: Decimal) -> Decimal`, which records a Payment and returns the new Balance.
+
+**Blocked by:** 01 (Account with Manual charges and Balance)
+
+**Status:** ready-for-agent
+
+- [ ] `pay` records a Payment and returns the new Balance (e.g. owing 5.00, paying 2.00 returns 3.00); `balance` agrees.
+- [ ] Paying exactly the Balance brings it to 0.
+- [ ] Paying more than the Balance raises `InvalidAmount`; so does any Payment when the Balance is 0. The Balance never goes negative.
+- [ ] `pay` raises `InvalidAmount` when the amount is zero, negative, has more than two decimal places, is NaN or infinite, or is not a `Decimal` (a `float` or an `int`), using the same rules as `add_charge`.
+- [ ] `pay` raises `MemberNotFound` for an unknown Member, ahead of `InvalidAmount` when both apply.
+- [ ] A refused `pay` leaves the Balance exactly as it was.
+- [ ] Tests go through the `LendingService` interface only. The existing suite still passes.
