+# 03: Fines on late return
+
+**What to build:** Returning a copy late automatically charges the Member a Fine on their Account. Fines are counted in Late days, priced by Material and capped per Loan, and children are never fined. Lateness on a Loan that is still out adds nothing until the copy comes back (ADR-0001). See `.scratch/overdue-fines/spec.md`; use the vocabulary in `GLOSSARY.md`, keeping "Late days" distinct from the report's "days overdue".
+
+`return_copy(copy_id)` keeps its signature and still returns the closed `Loan`.
+
+Rules:
+- **Late days**: days strictly after the due date, up to and including the return day, on which the library is open. Use the same open-day rule as due dates, so closed weekdays are defined in one place. Today that means Sundays never count.
+- **Rates** live in the policy module: book 0.25, DVD 1.00 per Late day. No grace period.
+- **Per-Loan cap**: the total fined for one Loan never exceeds its Title's replacement cost. Link each Fine to its Loan so the cap can be enforced per Loan when renewals arrive.
+- **Child exemption**: write it as one rule covering automatic Charges (Fines now, No-show fees later). Child returns are otherwise processed normally.
+- Shape the Fine calculation as "lateness of this Loan from its due date up to day X", so renewals can reuse it with X = the renewal day. Renewals themselves are out of scope.
+
+**Blocked by:** 01 (Account with Manual charges and Balance)
+
+**Status:** ready-for-agent
+
+- [ ] A book due Mon 23 Mar 2026 returned Mon 30 Mar 2026 is fined 1.50 (6 Late days; Sunday 29 Mar skipped).
+- [ ] A DVD due Mon 9 Mar 2026 returned Mon 16 Mar 2026 is fined 6.00 (7 calendar days, minus Sunday 15 Mar = 6 Late days).
+- [ ] A Loan spanning more than one Sunday skips each of them.
+- [ ] A return on the due date (or earlier) charges nothing and adds no Account entry; a return one Late day after the due date charges one day.
+- [ ] The Fine is capped at the Title's replacement cost: a DVD (replacement cost 12.00) returned 12 Late days late is fined 12.00, and one returned 20 Late days late is also fined 12.00.
+- [ ] A child Member's late return charges nothing and adds no Account entry, but still closes the Loan and puts the copy back on the shelf.
+- [ ] Several late returns by the same Member each add their own Fine, and the Balance is their sum (plus any Manual charges).
+- [ ] An overdue Loan that is still out adds nothing to the Balance.
+- [ ] `return_copy` still returns the closed Loan with `returned_on` set, and existing return behaviour and errors are unchanged.
+- [ ] The overdue report still shows calendar-day `days_overdue`; its existing tests pass unchanged.
+- [ ] Tests go through the `LendingService` interface, driven by `FixedClock`. The existing suite still passes.
