+# 04: Blocked from borrowing at checkout
+
+**What to build:** A Member whose Balance has reached the Borrowing limit (10.00) is Blocked from borrowing: checkout is refused until they pay the Balance below the limit. Returning copies and paying always work, even for a Member who is blocked. See `.scratch/overdue-fines/spec.md`; use the vocabulary in `GLOSSARY.md` and say "Blocked from borrowing", never a bare "Blocked".
+
+Add `AccountBlocked(LendingError)` to the lending errors module, raised by `checkout`. Put the Borrowing limit in the policy module as a threshold for one action, so that holds can later add a lower Hold limit (5.00) refused with the same `AccountBlocked`. Holds are out of scope here.
+
+**Blocked by:** 01 (Account with Manual charges and Balance), 02 (Payments), 03 (Fines on late return)
+
+**Status:** ready-for-agent
+
+- [ ] A Member with a Balance of exactly 10.00 cannot check out: `checkout` raises `AccountBlocked`.
+- [ ] A Member with a Balance of 9.99 can check out.
+- [ ] A refused checkout changes nothing: the copy stays available, no Loan is created, and the Member's open Loans are unchanged.
+- [ ] `checkout` checks in this order: Member exists (`MemberNotFound`) → copy exists (`CopyNotFound`) → Blocked from borrowing (`AccountBlocked`) → copy available (`CopyNotAvailable`) → loan limit (`LoanLimitReached`). In particular, a blocked Member asking for a copy already on loan gets `AccountBlocked`, and so does a blocked Member at their loan limit.
+- [ ] A Member who is Blocked from borrowing can still return copies, and the return still charges any Fine.
+- [ ] A Member who is Blocked from borrowing can still pay; once a Payment brings the Balance below 10.00 they can check out again.
+- [ ] A Fine charged by a late return counts toward the Borrowing limit straight away, e.g. a DVD returned 12 Late days late (Fine 12.00) blocks that Member's next checkout.
+- [ ] Manual charges count toward the Borrowing limit just like Fines.
+- [ ] Tests go through the `LendingService` interface, driven by `FixedClock`. The existing suite still passes.
