+
+**What to build:** Staff can renew an open Loan instead of returning and re-checking out the copy. The same Loan stays open and gets a new due date, a full loan period from the renewal day, and records how many times it has been renewed. The Member's loan history keeps showing one Loan. See `.scratch/renewals/spec.md`; use the vocabulary in `GLOSSARY.md`.
+
+Add `renewals: int` (default `0`, the last field) to `Loan`, `RenewalRefused(LendingError)` carrying the `loan_id` and a `reason` (shaped like `HoldNotAllowed`) to the lending errors module, and `renew(loan_id) -> Loan` to `LendingService`. The new due date uses the same due-date rule as checkout. This ticket checks only that the Loan exists and is open; the other refusal rules come in later tickets, in the order the spec gives.
