+# 05: Charge the lateness so far at renewal
+
+**What to build:** Renewing an overdue Loan charges a Fine for its lateness up to the renewal day, exactly as if the copy had come back that day, so lateness before a renewal is never lost (ADR-0001). Lateness after the renewal counts from the new due date. The Balance check comes before this Fine: a Member who owes nothing can renew an overdue Loan and then owes the Fine. See `.scratch/renewals/spec.md`; use the vocabulary in `GLOSSARY.md`.
+
+Reuse the existing Fine calculation with the renewal day as its end day, and post through the same automatic-charge path as a return, so the per-Loan cap, the child exemption and "no entry for a zero Fine" apply unchanged. Charge the Fine only after every check has passed, then set the new due date and count the renewal.
+
+**Blocked by:** 04 (Blocked from renewing: the Member must owe nothing)
+
+**Status:** ready-for-agent
+
+- [ ] A book due Monday 23 March renewed on Saturday 28 March adds a Fine of 1.25 (five Late days) to the Balance, and is then due Saturday 18 April.
+- [ ] Renewed on Monday 30 March instead, the Fine is 1.50: Sunday 29 March is not a Late day.
+- [ ] Renewing on or before the due date charges nothing.
+- [ ] The child Member renewing an overdue Loan is charged nothing, and the renewal is granted.
+- [ ] After the 28 March renewal, returning the copy on Tuesday 21 April adds only 0.50 (20 and 21 April), for 1.75 in total on the Loan.
+- [ ] The total fined for one Loan across the renewal and the return never exceeds the Title's replacement cost (use a cheap Title so the cap is reached in a few days).
+- [ ] A Member who owes nothing renews an overdue Loan and now owes its Fine; a second renewal, once inside the new window, raises `AccountBlocked` until they pay.
+- [ ] A renewal Fine counts toward the Borrowing limit and the Hold limit straight away.
+- [ ] A refused renewal of an overdue Loan charges nothing.
