new file mode 100644
index 0000000..bfea781
--- /dev/null
+++ b/GLOSSARY.md
@@ -0,0 +1,85 @@
+# Lending
+
+The circulation desk of the Elm Street public library: members, the catalogue, loans, and what members owe.
+
+## Language
+
+### Accounts
+
+**Account**:
+The record of what one Member has been charged and has paid. Every Member has exactly one.
+_Avoid_: Ledger, tab, member account
+
+**Charge**:
+An amount added to an Account that the Member owes.
+_Avoid_: Debt, penalty
+
+**Fine**:
+A Charge the library raises automatically when a Loan is returned or renewed late. The total fined for one Loan never exceeds its Title's replacement cost. Child Members are never fined.
+_Avoid_: Late fee, overdue charge, penalty
+
+**No-show fee**:
+A Charge raised automatically when a Ready Hold expires because the Member didn't collect it by its Pickup deadline. Child Members never pay it.
+_Avoid_: Hold fee, pickup penalty
+
+**Manual charge**:
+A Charge that staff add by hand, with a reason.
+_Avoid_: Adjustment, staff fee
+
+**Payment**:
+Money a Member hands over. It reduces their Balance and can never exceed it.
+_Avoid_: Credit, refund
+
+**Balance**:
+What a Member owes right now: all their Charges minus all their Payments. It is never negative. Lateness on a Loan that is still out does not count until the copy comes back or the Loan is renewed.
+_Avoid_: Debt, amount due, outstanding
+
+**Borrowing limit**:
+The Balance at or above which a Member can't borrow.
+
+**Hold limit**:
+The Balance at or above which a Member can't place a Hold. It is deliberately lower than the Borrowing limit. Holds already placed are unaffected.
+
+**Blocked from borrowing** / **Blocked from holds** / **Blocked from renewing**:
+A Member whose Balance has reached the Borrowing limit or the Hold limit, or who owes anything at all (for renewing). Always name the action: a Member can be blocked from holds and still borrow. Returning copies and paying are never blocked.
+_Avoid_: Blocked (on its own), suspended, barred
+
+### Holds
+
+**Hold**:
+A Member's place in line for a Title (never for a particular copy). A Member can place one only when every circulating copy of the Title is out, and not while they already have a Hold on it or a copy of it on loan. A Hold is waiting, then Ready, and ends fulfilled, cancelled or expired.
+_Avoid_: Reservation, request, waitlist entry
+
+**Hold queue**:
+The waiting and Ready Holds on one Title, oldest first. Every copy of the Title that becomes free goes to the oldest waiting Hold before it can go back on the shelf, so a Title never has a copy on the shelf while someone is waiting for it.
+_Avoid_: Waitlist, line
+
+**Ready**:
+A Hold for which a copy has been set aside on the Hold shelf. Only that Member can collect it.
+
+**Hold shelf**:
+Where a copy set aside for a Ready Hold waits. A copy on the Hold shelf is not available to anyone else.
+
+**Collect**:
+Borrowing the copy set aside for one's Ready Hold. This fulfils the Hold. All the usual borrowing rules still apply; if they refuse, the Hold stays Ready.
+_Avoid_: Pick up (as a verb for the system action)
+
+**Pickup deadline**:
+The last day a Ready Hold can be collected: seven days after the day the copy was set aside, moved to the Monday if that falls on a Sunday. The day after it, the Hold expires and the copy passes to the next waiting Hold.
+_Avoid_: Pickup time, hold expiry date
+
+### Renewals
+
+**Renewal**:
+Keeping the same Loan out longer: it gets a new due date, a full loan period from the day it is renewed, and any lateness so far is fined as if the copy came back that day. Only book Loans can be renewed, at most twice each, only within the Renewal window, and never while anyone has a waiting Hold on the Title. An overdue Loan can still be renewed.
+_Avoid_: Extension, re-checkout
+
+**Renewal window**:
+The days on which a Loan can be renewed: from five calendar days before its due date onwards, with no end. A Loan due Monday 23 March can be renewed from Wednesday 18 March.
+_Avoid_: Renewal period
+
+### Lateness
+
+**Late day**:
+A day after a Loan's due date, up to and including the day it comes back or is renewed, on which the library is open. Sundays are never Late days.
+_Avoid_: Days overdue (that is the calendar-day count on the overdue report)
