new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a5999a7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/adr/0001-fines-charged-on-return.md
@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+# Fines are charged when the copy comes back, not accrued
+
+A Loan that is still out and overdue adds nothing to the Member's Balance. Its Fine is charged in full on the day the copy is returned, and only then does it count toward being Blocked from borrowing. So a Member holding a DVD three months late is not blocked until they bring it back. We chose this over two alternatives:
+
+- counting the fine still accruing on open Loans in the Balance, which makes the Balance change every day without any event and makes "what you owe" a moving target at the desk;
+- blocking anyone with an overdue Loan, which is a separate rule we decided not to add.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Each late return adds its own Fine, and Fines add up on the Balance.
+- Renewals (planned) must charge the lateness so far as part of the renewal, counted as if the copy came back that day. Lateness before a renewal must never disappear, because under this rule nothing else will ever charge it.
